    "id": "10k_training_intermediate",
    "name": "10K Training: Intermediate",
    "author": "Hal Higdon",
    "version": "1.0",
    "created_at": null,
    "description": "THE SCHEDULE BELOW IS FOR INTERMEDIATE RUNNERS: individuals who want to improve their performances. What defines an Intermediate runner? You should be running five to six times a week, averaging 15-25 miles weekly training. You probably also should have run a half dozen or more races at distances between the 5K and the Half-Marathon. With ... Continue reading \"Intermediate\"",
